hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27677","Haddathana Ya'qub: Haddathana my father from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Sulayman ibn Suhaym narrated to me from Umayyah bint Abi al-Salt, from a woman of Banu Ghifar, and he named her to me, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among women of Banu Ghifar, and we said to him: O Messenger of Allah, we want to go out with you toward this destination of yours, while he was marching to Khaybar, so we may treat the wounded and help the Muslims as much as we can. So he said: Upon the blessing of Allah. She said: So we went out with him, and I was a young girl, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mounted me behind him upon the saddlebag of his mount. She said: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, dismounted toward dawn and made the camel kneel, and I dismounted from the saddlebag of his mount, and there was blood from me upon it, and it was the first menstruation I ever had. She said: So I withdrew to the camel and was shy. Then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw my state and saw the blood, he said: What is wrong with you? Perhaps you have menstruated. She said: I said: Yes. He said: Then set yourself right, take a vessel of water, cast salt therein, then wash what of blood touched the saddlebag, then return to your mount. She said: Then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, conquered Khaybar, he allotted to us from the fay', and he took this necklace that you see upon my neck and gave it to me and placed it with his hand upon my neck. By Allah, it shall never leave me. He said: And it was upon her neck until she died, then she bequeathed that it be buried with her. And she would not purify from a menstruation except that she put salt in her purification, and she bequeathed that salt be put in her washing when she died."
